Attempted to automate this by retrieving the sg’s as data, then concatenating that into the security group lists.


{noformat}data "aws_security_groups" "srep_prelive_sgs" {
  filter {
    name   = "tag:Name"
    values = ["srep-prelive-euc-1-main-node"]
  }

  provider = aws.platform-backend-prelive
}{noformat}

And then doing this:


{noformat}security_groups = concat(
[ "1234567890/sg-1a2b3c..." ],
data.aws_security_groups.srep_prelive.ids
){noformat}

However, the security groups are kept in a .tfvars file which currently don’t allow interpolation. To do so would require us to completely refactor how we currently write Security Groups across 15+ accounts.

Weighing up all of the factors:

# No buy-in from SRE Data/DBA
# The need for a human to still {{inv apply}} on each individual account
# It only requires a mass Find/Replace when we create a new account

I do not think currently the effort is worth the reward.

