Hey [~accountid:60ab8fc8efa79d00691a340f] [~accountid:6168449c2f6aed0068375106] [~accountid:60420da05290e70069b64add] 

This ticket has now been looked into and the attached documents have been reviewed. Essentially, you have two options here:

# You can proceed with liaising with the licensor for clarification on this bill and for the licensor to bare the cost of this water bill.
# You can pay the water bill (taking into account it is a cost over 18 months or so which is a charge around £50ish a month)

*Option 1* - As a first step you could seek to get some clarity from the licensor or the water company on how this charge is apportioned to Bolt. However, we need to be mindful of the way that we approach this situation given that we have a commercial relationship with the licensor that presumably we want to maintain. Please see suggested draft response which can be sent to the Licensor for clarification on why Bolt has been sent this bill.

+*_DRAFT RESPONSE TO BE SENT TO LICENSOR_*+ 

*Note:* *_(attach the water bill to email)_* 

{color:#ff5630}_Dear_{color}{color:#ff5630} *_[insert name]_*{color}

{color:#ff5630}_I hope you are well._{color}

{color:#ff5630}_We have received the attached letter dated  31 May 2023 requesting a sum of £961.59._{color}

{color:#ff5630}_Bolt is comfortable with contributing towards some run off costs, but at present we are seeking clarity on this bill. The attached bill appears to give no reference to Bolts Unit therefore we would like some further insight on how this bill is being apportioned between occupants. The licence agreement says that the licensor is contractually responsible for the upkeep and maintenance of the centre (as Bolt does not have any interest in the property, land, unit or the centre), and is responsible for incurring costs in respect of the centre (pursuant to clause 2 and 8 of the licence agreement). Taking this into consideration it is not clear why this bill has been addressed to Bolt._{color}

{color:#ff5630}_Moreover the bill doesn’t appear to be addressed to our Unit but instead the whole business park, therefore, it’s not clear how this is being apportioned. Bolt should not be paying costs in respect of the whole centre, do you have any knowledge of how this has happened?_{color}

{color:#ff5630}_We would kindly ask that you contact the water company to sort this matter out (noting that it is the licensors responsibility under this licence agreement), if not, please let us know._ {color}

{color:#ff5630}_We are happy to come to an arrangement that suits us both, however it is imperative that this fee has been apportioned to Bolt proper and fair._{color}

{color:#ff5630}_Should you wish to discuss further, please do not hesitate to contact us._ {color}

{color:#ff5630}_Thank you_{color}

{color:#ff5630}_Kind regards_{color}

{color:#ff5630}*[insert Bolt employee name]*{color}

*Option 2 -* Alternatively, the business could decide to go with option 2 for expediency, and you could arrange to pay this bill, taking into consideration that the cost comes to around £50 ish a month. 

Just to flag, if you decide to go with option 1 the above draft will assist in gaining clarity on this bill, however, if further correspondence regarding this bill is needed and you wish to dispute this bill further, you will need to take the lead on communicating with the licensor. This is because it will not be effective for the business for the legal team to get involved in this utilities dispute (as the bill is not high in value). 

I hope the above helps. Legal has now provided a review on this matter, however the approach you take (whether it is option 1 or option 2) is ultimately up to your team to decide. 

Happy to discuss any of the above in further detail, please do not hesitate to reach out to me on Slack. 

Thanks.

